{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And YHWH remembered</b> Every place where it says וה׳ — it is He and His court of justice, for the advocates argued on her behalf and said: if You do not give her a son now, then You delay the End that You decreed. And they answered them: ת' years from when he has seed, and he is now one hundred years old, and it must begin now. Another interpretation: they said, the daughters of Lot conceived from an act of prohibition with their father, and Sarah will not conceive from Abraham. Another interpretation: they said, she was secluded with Abimelech, and it is written: ואם טהורה היא ונקתה ונזרעה זרע (and if she is pure, she shall be cleared and sown with seed). And the reason she was not remembered after the seclusion with Pharaoh — because there it was manual contact, and the only thing lacking was intercourse." "<b>He remembered Sarah</b> in gematria: אף כל העקרות פקד (He also remembered all the barren women)."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:16:34.280340150Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}